WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.600
Dominoes Quick Starter. The Selfish Giant by Oscar Wilde 

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:11.550
Chapter 1. The Giant comes home.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:32.822
Every afternoon, when school finishes, the children play in the Giant's garden.

00:00:32.882 --> 00:00:38.554
It's a wonderful, big, green garden.

00:00:38.614 --> 00:00:46.686
There are beautiful flowers in it and twelve tall trees.

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:53.275
Birds like sitting and singing in these trees.

00:00:53.335 --> 00:01:00.306
The children often stop playing and listen to them.

00:01:00.366 --> 00:01:06.151
We're very happy here, they say.
 
00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:19.480
For seven years, the Giant stays away in Cornwall at the house of his friend, the Cornish Giant.

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:30.109
Then, one day, he comes home and he finds all the children in the garden.

00:01:30.169 --> 00:01:35.992
What are you doing here?

00:01:36.052 --> 00:01:42.174
he cries angrily, and the children run away.

00:01:42.194 --> 00:01:46.576
It's my garden,

00:01:46.636 --> 00:01:54.320
the Giant says. People must understand.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:02:02.474
And nobody can play here — only me!
 
00:02:02.534 --> 00:02:11.850
So he puts a wall around the garden with a big notice on it.

00:02:11.910 --> 00:02:15.448
NO CHILDREN.

00:02:15.508 --> 00:02:20.826
He is a very selfish Giant.

00:02:20.886 --> 00:02:26.257
Where can the children go now?

00:02:26.317 --> 00:02:30.700
They don't like playing in the road, 

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:37.400
so after school they walk around the wall 

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:51.300
and they look at it and they remember the beautiful garden behind it too.

00:02:51.450 --> 00:03:09.900
Chapter 2. Always winter. 

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:28.472
Then the spring comes.

00:03:28.532 --> 00:03:38.708
All over the country, there are spring flowers and little birds in the green trees.

00:03:38.768 --> 00:03:45.586
But in the Selfish Giant's garden, it stays winter.

00:03:45.646 --> 00:03:53.206
The birds don't want to sing in it because there are no children.

00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:57.579
The trees there stay dark.

00:03:57.638 --> 00:04:05.332
One beautiful flower puts its head up out of the ground.

00:04:05.392 --> 00:04:12.834
But it sees the notice and is very sorry for the children.

00:04:12.894 --> 00:04:20.446
So it goes back under the ground and sleeps again.

00:04:20.507 --> 00:04:24.928
Nobody is happy about this.

00:04:24.988 --> 00:04:29.610
Only the Snow and the Frost.

00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:35.573
Spring doesn't come to this garden, they cry.
 
00:04:35.633 --> 00:04:42.750
So we can live here all year!

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:49.800
The Snow puts her cold white coat on the ground 

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:56.675
and the Frost puts silver on the dark trees.

00:04:56.735 --> 00:05:04.450
They tell the North Wind, You must stay with us.

00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:10.732
So he comes in his big brown coat.

00:05:10.792 --> 00:05:17.114
He makes lots of noise up and down the garden.

00:05:17.174 --> 00:05:23.000
And he moves things here and there all day.

00:05:23.067 --> 00:05:29.132
This is wonderful! he cries.
 
00:05:29.192 --> 00:05:34.700
Let's ask the Hail here too.

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:38.839
So the Hail comes.

00:05:38.899 --> 00:05:48.722
Every day he sits on the roof of the Giant's big old house.

00:05:48.782 --> 00:05:56.996
He never stops hitting it noisily hour after hour.

00:05:57.056 --> 00:06:02.168
His suit is the colour of smoke.

00:06:02.227 --> 00:06:09.999
And cold smoke comes from his mouth when he opens it.

00:06:10.059 --> 00:06:15.950
The Selfish Giant sits at his window.

00:06:16.010 --> 00:06:22.072
He looks out at his cold white garden.

00:06:22.131 --> 00:06:26.873
I don't understand, he says.

00:06:26.933 --> 00:06:31.504
The spring's very late this year.

00:06:31.564 --> 00:06:34.326
When is it coming?

00:06:34.386 --> 00:06:56.500
And when is this winter finishing?

00:06:56.560 --> 00:07:19.700
Chapter 3. The hole in the wall. 

00:07:19.760 --> 00:07:26.686
The spring and the summer never come to the Giant's garden.

00:07:26.746 --> 00:07:33.851
The autumn brings golden apples to most people's gardens.

00:07:33.911 --> 00:07:39.814
But to the Giant's garden, she brings nothing.

00:07:39.874 --> 00:07:45.316
I don't give to selfish people, she says.

00:07:45.376 --> 00:07:50.094
So it is always winter there.

00:07:50.154 --> 00:08:00.395
And the North Wind, the Hail, the Frost and the Snow run about in it.

00:08:00.455 --> 00:08:14.331
One morning, when the Giant opens his eyes in bed, he hears some music.

00:08:14.391 --> 00:08:18.354
That's beautiful! he cries.
 
00:08:18.414 --> 00:08:20.586
But what is it?

00:08:20.645 --> 00:08:26.040
A little bird is singing near his window.

00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:27.812
That's all.

00:08:27.871 --> 00:08:38.771
But after the long winter in his garden, the Giant can't remember the noise very well.

00:08:38.831 --> 00:08:45.166
Then the Hail stops hitting the roof.

00:08:45.226 --> 00:08:49.595
And the North Wind is quiet.

00:08:49.655 --> 00:09:00.064
Suddenly, a wonderful perfume comes to the Giant through the open window.

00:09:00.124 --> 00:09:06.526
The spring's here at last, I think! he cries.
 
00:09:06.586 --> 00:09:11.668
Then he gets up and looks out.

00:09:11.728 --> 00:09:15.460
What a wonderful thing!

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:24.419
The children are coming into the garden through a little hole in the wall.

00:09:24.479 --> 00:09:28.430
And they are sitting in the trees.

00:09:28.490 --> 00:09:35.213
And the trees are happy because the children are back.

00:09:35.273 --> 00:09:42.505
They begin to blossom and move their arms about.

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:47.817
The birds are singing happily in the sky.

00:09:47.877 --> 00:09:54.328
The flowers are coming out of the ground and laughing.

00:09:54.388 --> 00:10:03.332
But far across the garden, in one corner, it isn't spring.

00:10:03.392 --> 00:10:08.083
A young boy is standing there.

00:10:08.143 --> 00:10:17.586
There is frost and snow on his tree, and he cannot get up into it.

00:10:17.646 --> 00:10:22.227
So he is crying.

00:10:22.287 --> 00:10:56.000
Chapter 4. The boy in the tree. 

00:10:56.100 --> 00:10:59.750
Get up, little boy,

00:10:59.810 --> 00:11:04.304
says the tree in that corner of the garden.

00:11:04.364 --> 00:11:11.700
And it puts its branches nearer the ground for the young boy.

00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:18.936
But he is very little, and he can't get on them.

00:11:18.996 --> 00:11:23.900
The Giant watches from his window, 

00:11:23.960 --> 00:11:29.812
and his cold heart is suddenly warmer.

00:11:29.873 --> 00:11:34.345
Now I see! he cries.
 
00:11:34.405 --> 00:11:41.880
The spring doesn't come here because I'm selfish.

00:11:41.940 --> 00:11:45.612
He is truly sorry.

00:11:45.672 --> 00:11:49.159
I know, he says.

00:11:49.219 --> 00:11:59.410
I can put the little boy up in the tree and knock down the wall.

00:11:59.470 --> 00:12:07.414
Then the children can always play in my garden.

00:12:07.474 --> 00:12:16.530
So he goes quietly down to his front door and he opens it.

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:22.276
Then he goes out into the garden.

00:12:22.336 --> 00:12:29.400
When the children see him, they are very afraid.

00:12:29.460 --> 00:12:33.834
So they all run away.

00:12:33.894 --> 00:12:39.206
And it is winter in the garden again.

00:12:39.266 --> 00:12:46.062
But the little boy has his head in his hands. 

00:12:46.126 --> 00:12:50.162
He can't see the Giant.

00:12:50.222 --> 00:12:58.078
So the Giant goes very quietly over to him.

00:12:58.137 --> 00:13:04.100
He takes the little boy carefully in his hand 

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:09.201
and he puts him up in the tree.

00:13:09.261 --> 00:13:20.020
At once the tree blossoms and the birds come and sing in it.

00:13:20.080 --> 00:13:31.482
Then the little boy puts his arms around the Giant's neck and he kisses him.

00:13:31.542 --> 00:13:37.800
When the other children see this, they understand. 

00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:42.892
The Giant isn't bad anymore.

00:13:42.952 --> 00:13:51.109
So they run back into the garden and the spring comes with them.

00:13:51.169 --> 00:13:56.374
It's your garden now, little children,

00:13:56.434 --> 00:13:58.756
the Giant says.

00:13:58.816 --> 00:14:23.000
Then he takes a big axe and he knocks down the wall.

00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:46.700
Chapter 5. The most beautiful flowers. 

00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:54.466
At twelve o'clock that day, the people are going to the shops.

00:14:54.526 --> 00:14:58.038
They see the Giant.

00:14:58.098 --> 00:15:06.020
He is playing with the children in the most beautiful garden.

00:15:06.079 --> 00:15:11.611
All day long, the children play.

00:15:11.671 --> 00:15:18.972
In the evening, they come and say goodbye to the Giant.

00:15:19.032 --> 00:15:23.334
But where's your little friend?

00:15:23.394 --> 00:15:25.574
he asks them.

00:15:25.634 --> 00:15:35.446
The young boy is the Giant's favourite because he remembers the child's kiss.

00:15:35.506 --> 00:15:38.216
We don't know,

00:15:38.276 --> 00:15:41.717
one of the children answers.

00:15:41.777 --> 00:15:45.018
He isn't here now.

00:15:45.078 --> 00:15:50.370
Well, he must come again tomorrow.

00:15:50.430 --> 00:15:54.040
Please tell him that,

00:15:54.100 --> 00:15:59.178
the Giant says. Where does he live?

00:15:59.238 --> 00:16:04.841
We're not sure, a different child says.
 
00:16:04.901 --> 00:16:08.022
We don't know him.

00:16:08.082 --> 00:16:15.336
When the Giant hears this, he is very sad.

00:16:15.397 --> 00:16:26.774
Every afternoon, when school finishes, the children come and play with the Giant.

00:16:26.834 --> 00:16:36.219
But the Giant's favourite, the little boy, never comes back.

00:16:36.280 --> 00:16:42.050
The Giant is very nice to all the children, 

00:16:42.110 --> 00:16:49.036
but he wants to see his first little friend again.

00:16:49.096 --> 00:16:53.526
He speaks about him a lot.

00:16:53.586 --> 00:16:58.928
I would like to see him again one day,

00:16:58.988 --> 00:17:02.829
he often says.

00:17:02.889 --> 00:17:11.292
After many years, the Giant is old and weak.

00:17:11.352 --> 00:17:15.323
He cannot play anymore.

00:17:15.383 --> 00:17:21.850
So he sits in a nice big chair.

00:17:21.910 --> 00:17:26.634
And he watches the children's games.

00:17:26.694 --> 00:17:32.580
He looks at his garden happily too.

00:17:32.640 --> 00:17:39.006
I have many beautiful flowers, he says.

00:17:39.066 --> 00:18:04.600
But the children are the most beautiful flowers of all.

00:18:04.660 --> 00:18:25.200
Chapter 6. The wounds of love. 

00:18:25.300 --> 00:18:37.092
One winter morning, when he is getting up, the Giant looks out of his window.

00:18:37.152 --> 00:18:42.526
The winter doesn't matter to him now.

00:18:42.586 --> 00:18:50.200
The spring is sleeping at that time of the year, he knows, 

00:18:50.260 --> 00:18:57.214
and the flowers are in their beds under the ground.

00:18:57.274 --> 00:19:04.104
Suddenly he sees something wonderful.

00:19:04.164 --> 00:19:11.610
Can it be true? he cries.
 
00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:26.817
Far across the garden in one corner, there is a tree with beautiful white blossoms all over it.

00:19:26.877 --> 00:19:34.017
There are silver apples on its golden branches.

00:19:34.077 --> 00:19:43.480
And the little boy, his favourite, is standing under the tree.

00:19:43.540 --> 00:19:48.322
He is all in white.

00:19:48.382 --> 00:19:59.705
The Giant runs down to his front door and out into the garden.

00:19:59.765 --> 00:20:05.688
He goes quickly across it to the child.

00:20:05.748 --> 00:20:14.004
But when he comes near, his face is suddenly angry.

00:20:14.064 --> 00:20:19.487
Where do these wounds come from?

00:20:19.547 --> 00:20:30.390
he cries, because there, on the boy's hands, are the wounds of two nails,

00:20:30.450 --> 00:20:38.326
and the wounds of two nails are on his little feet.

00:20:38.385 --> 00:20:44.150
Who is guilty of this?

00:20:44.210 --> 00:20:53.566
Tell me, and I can take my big sword and kill him.

00:20:53.586 --> 00:21:03.968
No, the child answers, because these are the wounds of love.
 
00:21:04.028 --> 00:21:08.022
Who are you?

00:21:08.082 --> 00:21:16.556
the Giant says quietly, and he kneels before the child.

00:21:16.616 --> 00:21:24.890
Then the child smiles at the Giant and tells him, 

00:21:24.950 --> 00:21:32.320
You remember me from before, here in your garden.

00:21:32.380 --> 00:21:43.792
And today, you are coming away with me to my garden — Paradise.
 
00:21:43.852 --> 00:21:56.850
When the children run into the garden that afternoon, they find the Giant under the tree.

00:21:56.910 --> 00:22:00.098
He is dead now.

00:22:00.158 --> 00:22:20.428
And there are beautiful white blossoms all over him.